# `a2a whatsnew`: renders the embedded release-notes corpus — no space, no
# config needed. This shared t3 test binary is built with -X
# main.version=$A2A_STAMPED_VERSION (main_test.go's harnessStampedVersion,
# pinned to contract.ContractPublicationFloor for B33 — see main_test.go).
# Whatever the selected release range turns out to be for that stamp, the
# independently loaded current known-issues list must still be present in
# text and JSON (AttachCurrentKnownIssues always attaches it to the newest
# selected release, or to a bare carrier release if the range is empty).
# "0.1.0" below is a LITERAL, not the harness's stamp: it is an arbitrary
# --since value chosen to sit below every entry in the corpus (the lowest
# shipped release is 0.2.0), so it exercises `--since` picking up the WHOLE
# corpus range, deliberately independent of whatever version this harness
# stamps into the binary. Rich rendering (digest text, impact ordering,
# action-scope directives, JSON shape) is covered by
# internal/cli/cmd_whatsnew_test.go and internal/mcp/tools_whatsnew_test.go
# against a fixed, injected corpus.
exec a2a whatsnew
stdout 'KNOWN ISSUE'
stdout 'The macOS companion remains ad-hoc signed'

exec a2a whatsnew --since 0.1.0
stdout 'KNOWN ISSUE'
stdout 'The macOS companion remains ad-hoc signed'

exec a2a whatsnew --since 0.1.0 --json
stdout '"id": "KI-MACOS-ADHOC-SIGNING"'
